<title>USA: Honeywell completes Measurex acquisition.</title>
<headline>Honeywell completes Measurex acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honeywell Inc said Friday it completed its previously announced acquisition of Measurex Corp.</p>
<p>Former Measurex stockholders are entitled to receive $35 in cash for each of their shares. This is the same price paid by Honeywell Acquisition Corp based on its recently completed cash tender offer for all outstanding Measurex shares.</p>
<p>Honeywell's existing pulp-and-paper business will be merged into Measurex, based in Cupertino, Calif., and the new business will be renamed Honeywell-Measurex. Measurex provides systems used to control papermaking processes.</p>
<p>	  ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
